:11379","provisional_status":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"done","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"open","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"7","steps_done":"3"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 11379\nDESIGNATING OFFICIALS TO ACT AS COMMISSIONER OF THE \nDISTRICT OF COLUMBIA\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by section 301(d) of \nReorganization Plan No. 3 of 1967 (32 F.R. 11671), it is ordered that \nthe following-designated officials of the District of Columbia shall, \nin the order of succession indicated, act as Commissioner of the \nDistrict of Columbia during the absence from duty or disability of \nthe Commissioner of the District of Columbia or in the event of a \nvacancy in the office of Commissioner:\n(1) The Assistant to the Commissioner of the District of Columbia \nprovided for in section 302 of Reorganization Plan No. 3 of 1967.\n(2) The Corporation Counsel of the District of Columbia.\nT h e W h ite H ouse,\nNovember 8,1967.\n[F.R. Doc. 67-13369; Filed, Nov. 9, 1967; 9:54 a.m.]","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-11379-cfbb9bce42.txt","sha256":"2440dfd54a5bc82a8259d079189155466e29a5efabaa462fd225952fd3e06d49","source":{"line":2341,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"e2305856f45e9940e58e74685fa307a4568c32da210772fbbf28e323f9d51af4"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:11379\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1967-11-10/pdf/FR-1967-11-10.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: cfbb9bce42a94b61a8e8b6a9a7f1368eb7c45f10cb7a0781e484dd19b458ca7c\nLocation: 32 FR 15625, PDF pages 5-5 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 5 of 48 ===\nPresidential Documents\nTitle 3— THE PRESIDENT\nExecutive Order 11379\nDESIGNATING OFFICIALS TO ACT AS COMMISSIONER OF THE \nDISTRICT OF COLUMBIA\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by section 301(d) of \nReorganization Plan No. 3 of 1967 (32 F.R. 11671), it is ordered that \nthe following-designated officials of the District of Columbia shall, \nin the order of succession indicated, act as Commissioner of the \nDistrict of Columbia during the absence from duty or disability of \nthe Commissioner of the District of Columbia or in the event of a \nvacancy in the office of Commissioner:\n(1) The Assistant to the Commissioner of the District of Columbia \nprovided for in section 302 of Reorganization Plan No. 3 of 1967.\n(2) The Corporation Counsel of the District of Columbia.\nT h e W h ite H ouse,\nNovember 8,1967.\n[F.R. Doc. 67-13369; Filed, Nov. 9, 1967; 9:54 a.m.]\nF E D E R A L  R E G IS T E R , V O L. 32, NO. 219— F R ID A Y , N O V E M B E R  10, 1967\n","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_11379.txt","sha256":"37a9c9767cecfd943acf4e4caac96c7f6dcd019b59ab33f860ac86d32cb8eb22","source":{"line":1236,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5fe50b5819e815d336968efadbdfb85275af249b65257e4be657e53ee24030ba"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Wanted: opus-refetch:ee87f6027e6f3902a09e1907d991c5d40fab8b3931446ccf7d8a558325636ebb\nCited by: EO:10128, EO:11379, EO:11401, EO:11571, EO:11815, EO:6868, EO:7784A, EO:8033, EO:9344, EO:9916\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/STATUTE-87/pdf/STATUTE-87-Pg774.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: ee87f6027e6f3902a09e1907d991c5d40fab8b3931446ccf7d8a558325636ebb\nLocation: STATUTE-87-Pg774.pdf PDF pages 1-40 of 63\nMachine-extracted text (from a scan's text layer for older documents). Not an authenticated transcription; check the PDF.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 63 ===\n774 PUBLIC LAW 93-198-DEC. 24, 1973 [87 STAT. \nDecember 24, 1973 \n[S. 1435] \nDistrict of \nColumbia Self-\nGovemment and \nGovernmental Re­\norganization Act. \nPublic Law 93-198 - -\nAN ACT \nTo reorganize the governmental structure of the District of Columbia, to provide \na charter for local government in the District of Columbia subject to acceptance \nby a majority of the registered qualilled electors in the District of Columbia, to \ndelegate certain legislative powers to the local government, to implement \ncertain recommendations of the Commission on the Organization of the Govern­\nment of the District of Columbia, and for other purposes. \nBe it enacted hy the Senate and House of Refvesentatives of the \nUnited States of Amenca m Congress assembled, \nTABLE OF CONTENTS \nTITLE I—SHORT TITLE, PURPOSES, AND DEFINITIONS \nSec. 101. Short title. \nSec. 1()2. Statement of puiiwues. \nSec. 103. Deflnitions. \nTITLE II—GOVERNMENTAL REO","path":"jobs/source-ladder/output/texts/opus-refetch_ee87f6027e6f3902a09e1907d991c5d40fab8b3931446ccf7d8a558325636ebb_fe267a16aa.txt","sha256":"5c5b5ca8c07eabafb315a5cd4a5ebafea6259b201405b5a033001b06e73be320","source":{"line":111,"path":"jobs/source-ladder/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"b35594a1b8bc09d01c15125758094904db0b3f7f874e524896a1a231466e45ea"}}]}
